Service Commission finds that the person is unfit for the office of judge or that the judge has committed an act unbecoming of that office, and a motion to remove that judge from office is submitted to the People's Majlis and passed by a two-thirds majority of the members present and voting at the sitting of the Majlis;

Whereas, following the advice given by the Judicial Service Commission to remove two Supreme Court justices from office, the removal of those two justices from office was passed by the votes of 68 members of the People's Majlis on 14 May 2025;

Whereas, as the evidence and circumstantial evidence found in the investigation of the case submitted by the Anti-Corruption Commission (ACC) to the Maldives Police Service did not indicate that a criminal offence had been committed, and following the Prosecutor General's Office's decision not to press charges in this case, the case has now been filed away by the Police Service;

Whereas the Prosecutor General's Office's decision not to press charges reveals that the Supreme Court justices were removed from office on the basis of allegations without any evidentiary basis;

Whereas it is considered that, it being revealed, after the Judicial Service Commission removed justices of the country's highest court from office solely on the basis of a suspicion of an offence, that no criminal offence is considered to have been committed is [?], the Judicial Service Commission must bear responsibility for this and must be held accountable for it;

